cory: Quick thread to consolidate the last week of tickets: we need a short, concrete section in our SDK docs that covers (a) how our fetch adapter works, (b) typing pitfalls for TS users, and (c) bundler rules so undici never ends up in browser/edge bundles. Thoughts?

maria: Strong +1. We should include both the runtime adapter and an explanation of why it's dynamic-imported. Many customers see `import undici` in their bundle analyzer and get spooked.

jules: Agreed. Also surface the minimal tsconfig changes people need. I've seen projects fail on `Request`/`Response` types because they exclude "dom". Offer an example and a one-line troubleshooting checklist.

cory: Draft proposal for the docs: - A single paragraph describing the adapter: "uses globalThis.fetch if present; otherwise lazy-loads undici at runtime; throws a clear error that suggests `npm i undici` or running on Node 18+." - A tiny code example showing a cached dynamic loader. - TS troubleshooting snippet. - Bundler tips (esbuild/webpack/rollup) and how conditional exports + sideEffects=false help. - CI checks we run (bundle-size for edge target, Node 18/20 smoke).

maria: Example loader I want to include (keeps bundlers happy by avoiding static imports):
```ts
// runtime/fetch-shim.ts
let cached: typeof fetch | undefined;
export async function getFetch(): Promise<typeof fetch> {
  if (cached) return cached;
  if ((globalThis as any).fetch) {
    cached = globalThis.fetch;
    return cached;
  }
  // dynamic import so bundlers don't statically include undici
  try {
    const mod = await import('undici');
    cached = (mod as any).fetch;
    return cached;
  } catch (e) {
    // CJS fallback for older consumers
    try {
      // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-var-requires
      const req = require('undici');
      cached = req.fetch;
      return cached;
    } catch (e2) {
      throw new Error('No fetch available. Install undici (npm i undici) or run on a runtime that provides fetch.');
    }
  }
}
```

jules: Nice. Add a tiny example showing how to pass a custom fetch into the client for tracing or custom headers:```js
// app.js
import { createClient } from '@redwood-inference/sdk';
import { getFetch } from './runtime/fetch-shim';
(async () => {
  const f = await getFetch();
  const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.RI_KEY, fetch: f });
})();
```

maria: TS notes for docs: show `tsconfig.json` snippet and mention that some users prefer adding `npm i -D @types/undici` if they explicitly install undici. Also call out that Node 18+ includes fetch types if tsconfig target >= es2022 in some setups, but we can't rely on that across all toolchains. Snippet:```json
{ "compilerOptions": { "lib": ["es2021", "dom"], "target": "es2021" } }
```

cory: Bundler guidance to include: - Make undici optionalDependency or peer (we decided optionalDependency). - Use dynamic import pattern above so esbuild/webpack/rollup don't include undici by default. - For consumers who want to force a different implementation, show how to alias in bundlers (example: esbuild --define:globalThis.fetch=... or webpack resolve.alias). - Recommend package.json conditional exports so edge builds pick web entry automatically. Example exports block:```json
"exports": { 
  ".": { "import": "./dist/esm/index.js", "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js" }
}
```

jules: Also document runtime matrix and CI: Node 18, Node 20, Next.js server & edge, Vercel Edge, Cloudflare Workers, Bun (experimental), Deno (experimental). Add a small bundle-size job that builds an edge-targeted bundle and runs `bundlesize` to ensure undici not included.

maria: Edge gotcha: AbortSignal semantics are inconsistent. Recommend we expose `utils/newSignal()` in SDK docs and state explicitly: "create a fresh signal per attempt; do not reuse signals across retries." Also call out that streaming semantics differ between Node streams and web ReadableStreams.

cory: Action items from this thread: (1) I'll add the runtime fetch shim and wire it as the SDK default (no top-level undici import). (2) Maria, can you add the tsconfig troubleshooting and @types/undici note to quickstart? (3) Jules, add bundler tips + example alias for esbuild/webpack to docs. (4) CI: add edge bundle-size check and runtime matrix.

build-bot: CI #2551: build and packaging tests passed on Node 18/20; edge bundle-size job created (pending).

maria: One more small UX improvement: include a one-liner troubleshooting section at the end of quickstart: "If you see `fetch is not defined` -> add `npm i undici` for Node <18 or run on a runtime with fetch; ensure tsconfig includes `dom` in libs for TypeScript."

jules: I'll draft the docs PR after lunch and tag you both. Let's keep the code example minimal so it's easy to copy into sample-apps.

cory: Great. If we keep the adapter tiny and lazy we'll avoid most of the bundle surprises. Thanks folks — please drop any extra tips in this thread before I open the PR.
